# Cursor Rules

`AGENTS.md` is the binding engineering policy for this repository. Read it before any task and follow it end to end; if any skill, template, or prompt conflicts with it, `AGENTS.md` wins. This file adds no policy of its own.

Before implementing:

- Map the target flow via `docs/REPO_MAP.md` + `docs/DOMAIN_MAP.md`.
- Preserve the layer model and dependency direction from `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`.
- Treat `docs/ARCHITECTURE_REFACTOR_NEXT.md` as the only active roadmap authority.

Restated here because they are the most frequently violated rules (canonical wording in `AGENTS.md`):

- Run the full quality gate sequence after changes, one command at a time, and report the executed checks; do not finish on code edits alone.
- Never run `php artisan test` or `npm run test` in parallel (shared `database/testing.sqlite`).
- No temporary hacks, no unrelated refactors, no weakening of guardrail tests or their allowlists.
- After each completed logical block, update `docs/REFACTORING_EXECUTION_PLAN.md` with the work and the checks run.
